 ### 2010 — mac-keyvault T2 rev2: an embedded interface method is a guard bypass, and a bytes-only policy check belongs before the backend boundary
 - FINDING (review rev1 F1): `GuardedStore` embeds `Backend` and overrode `Create`/`Delete`/`UpdateTag` only; Go promoted `Backend.Sign` unchanged, so the integration guard that keeps tests inside `works.relux.mac-keyvault.key.test.*` did not cover the private-key operation added in T2 — the rev1 results artifact claimed it did. Fix: `(*GuardedStore).Sign` calls `guard` first; `TestGuardedStoreRefusesNonTestLabels` now drives `Sign` with a signing-capable production label (a leak would return a real signature, not `ErrNotFound`) and a test-label positive control. Rule recorded in the type comment: every mutating or private-key-using `Backend` method must be overridden on the guard; embedding is where bypasses come from.
 - FINDING (review rev1 F2): `runVerify` refused high-S after `Manager.PublicKeyFor` → `Backend.List`, so a malleable signature by label caused a Security call before the policy refusal, against the T1 "no backend call before validation" guard. The check only needs the parsed `(r, s)`, so it now sits directly after `ParseSignature`, before the `--spki` file read and before the address is resolved; the refusal envelope carries the digest/format/low_s inputs but no key fields. `TestRunVerifyHighSRefusedBeforeStore` prepares signatures with `crypto/ecdsa` (never via `run(sign)`), uses a fresh recording store holding the key, and asserts zero calls plus two ordering witnesses (absent address and absent `--spki` path are still `high_s_refused`, not `not_found`/usage). Mutants M16 (rev1 order), M17 (early gate DER-only), M18 (early gate `--spki`-only) are all killed; M4 from rev1 only proved the raw refusal existed.
